(>> 2.1 Electrochemical Cells, Electrode Potentials & Nernst Equation) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Electrochemistry investigates chemical-electrical energy conversions and metallic) Tj
T*
(degradation interfaces.) Tj
T*
(* Galvanic \(Voltaic\) Cell: Converts spontaneous chemical redox free energy into) Tj
T*
(electrical work \(e.g., Daniell Cell: Zn\(s\) | Zn2+\(aq\) || Cu2+\(aq\) | Cu\(s\)\).) Tj
T*
(- Anode \(Oxidation\): Zn -> Zn2+ + 2 e- \(Negative terminal\).) Tj
T*
(- Cathode \(Reduction\): Cu2+ + 2 e- -> Cu \(Positive terminal\).) Tj
T*
(- Cell Potential: E_cell = E_cathode - E_anode.) Tj
T*
(* The Nernst Equation: Quantifies electrode and cell potentials under non-standard) Tj
T*
(concentrations:) Tj
T*
(E = E^0 - [ \(R * T\) / \(n * F\) ] * ln\(Q\) = E^0 - [ 0.0591 / n ] * log10\( [Products] /) Tj
T*
([Reactants] \) at 298 K.) Tj
T*
(* Reference Electrodes:) Tj
T*
(- Standard Hydrogen Electrode \(SHE\): Primary standard assigned E^0 = 0.000 V: Pt |) Tj
T*
(H2\(g, 1 atm\) | H+\(aq, 1 M\).) Tj
T*
(- Saturated Calomel Electrode \(SCE\): Secondary reference: Hg | Hg2Cl2\(s\) |) Tj
T*
(KCl\(sat\). E = +0.2422 V vs. SHE at 25 deg C.) Tj
T*
(- Silver/Silver Chloride Electrode: Ag | AgCl\(s\) | KCl\(sat\). E = +0.199 V vs. SHE.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
