/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 2.2 Corrosion Mechanisms: Chemical \(Dry\) vs. Electrochemical \(Wet\)) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Corrosion is the unintentional, spontaneous destruction of metals by chemical or) Tj
T*
(electrochemical reaction with surrounding environment.) Tj
T*
(* Dry \(Chemical\) Corrosion: Direct reaction with dry gases \(O2, Cl2, SO2\) at elevated) Tj
T*
(temperatures:) Tj
T*
(- Pilling-Bedworth Rule: Predicts whether an oxide layer is protective. P-B Ratio) Tj
T*
(= Volume of Metal Oxide formed / Volume of Metal consumed:) Tj
T*
(If P-B Ratio < 1 \(e.g., Na, K, Mg, Ca\): Oxide film is porous, cracked, and) Tj
T*
(non-protective; corrosion continues unabated.) Tj
T*
(If P-B Ratio >= 1 to 2 \(e.g., Al, Cr, Ni, Ti\): Oxide film is continuous, dense,) Tj
T*
(non-porous, and self-passivating.) Tj
T*
(If P-B Ratio > 2 \(e.g., Fe, Ta\): Compressive stresses cause buckling and spalling of the) Tj
T*
(oxide coat.) Tj
T*
(* Wet \(Electrochemical\) Corrosion: Occurs in aqueous media via separate micro-anode) Tj
T*
(and micro-cathode sites:) Tj
T*
(- Anodic Reaction: Metal dissolves: M -> M^{n+} + n e-.) Tj
T*
(- Cathodic Reaction \(depends on environment\):) Tj
T*
(1. Hydrogen Evolution \(in acidic media\): 2 H+ + 2 e- -> H2 \(g\).) Tj
T*
(2. Oxygen Absorption \(in neutral/alkaline media\): O2 + 2 H2O + 4 e- -> 4 OH-.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
