T*
(* Galvanic Corrosion: Two dissimilar metals in electrical contact in an electrolyte;) Tj
T*
(the more active metal \(lower reduction potential\) corrodes rapidly while the more) Tj
T*
(noble metal is protected.) Tj
T*
(* Differential Aeration Corrosion: Metal exposed to varying oxygen concentrations;) Tj
T*
(poorly aerated areas become anodic and corrode, while well-aerated areas act as) Tj
T*
(cathodes \(e.g., pitting corrosion, waterline corrosion\).) Tj
T*
(* Corrosion Protection:) Tj
T*
(- Sacrificial Anode Cathodic Protection: Structure connected to a more active) Tj
T*
(sacrificial metal \(Zn, Mg, Al\).) Tj
T*
(- Impressed Current Cathodic Protection: External DC source drives electrons into) Tj
T*
(protected structure via inert anodes \(graphite, platinized titanium\).) Tj
