([SOLVED PROBLEM 1: Cell EMF and Equilibrium Constant via Nernst Equation]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Calculate the EMF of the following galvanic cell at 25 deg C \(298 K\):) Tj
T*
(Zn\(s\) | Zn2+\(0.01 M\) || Cu2+\(0.1 M\) | Cu\(s\).) Tj
T*
(Standard potentials: E^0\(Zn2+/Zn\) = -0.76 V, E^0\(Cu2+/Cu\) = +0.34 V. Also calculate the) Tj
T*
(equilibrium constant K_c.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Overall Cell Reaction and Standard EMF E^0_cell:) Tj
T*
(Anode: Zn\(s\) -> Zn2+\(aq\) + 2 e-.) Tj
T*
(Cathode: Cu2+\(aq\) + 2 e- -> Cu\(s\).) Tj
T*
(Net: Zn\(s\) + Cu2+\(aq\) -> Zn2+\(aq\) + Cu\(s\). \(n = 2 electrons transferred\).) Tj
T*
(E^0_cell = E^0_cathode - E^0_anode = +0.34 - \(-0.76\) = +1.10 Volts.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Apply Nernst Equation:) Tj
T*
(E_cell = E^0_cell - [ 0.0591 / n ] * log10\( [Zn2+] / [Cu2+] \)) Tj
T*
(E_cell = 1.10 - [ 0.0591 / 2 ] * log10\( 0.01 / 0.1 \) = 1.10 - 0.02955 * log10\( 0.10 \)) Tj
T*
(Since log10\(0.1\) = -1:) Tj
T*
(E_cell = 1.10 - 0.02955 * \(-1\) = 1.10 + 0.02955 = +1.1296 Volts.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate Equilibrium Constant K_c:) Tj
T*
(At equilibrium, E_cell = 0: E^0_cell = [ 0.0591 / n ] * log10\(K_c\)) Tj
T*
(1.10 = \(0.0591 / 2\) * log10\(K_c\) => log10\(K_c\) = 1.10 / 0.02955 = 37.225.) Tj
T*
(K_c = 10^{37.225} = 1.68 * 10^37.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Cell EMF is +1.130 V, and the massive K_c indicates virtually complete) Tj
T*
(thermodynamic conversion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
