T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: An underground steel bioreactor tank exhibits an anodic corrosion leakage) Tj
T*
(current of 0.50 Amperes for 365 days. Assuming iron dissolves as Fe -> Fe2+ + 2 e- \(Fe:) Tj
T*
(55.85 g/mol, F = 96,485 C/mol\), calculate: \(1\) Total mass of steel lost to corrosion in) Tj
T*
(kilograms, \(2\) Mass of sacrificial Magnesium anode required to protect the tank for 5) Tj
T*
(years at 0.5A \(Mg: 24.31 g/mol, n = 2\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Total Charge Transferred Q in 1 Year:) Tj
T*
(t = 365 days = 365 * 24 * 3600 = 31,536,000 seconds.) Tj
T*
(Q = I * t = 0.50 A * 31,536,000 s = 15,768,000 Coulombs.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Mass of Iron Dissolved via Faraday's Law:) Tj
T*
(m = \(M * I * t\) / \(n * F\) = \(55.85 * 15,768,000\) / \(2 * 96,485\) = 880,642,800 / 192,970) Tj
T*
(= 4,563.6 grams = 4.56 kg of steel.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Required Sacrificial Magnesium Mass for 5 Years:) Tj
T*
(t_5yr = 5 * 31,536,000 = 157,680,000 seconds.) Tj
T*
(m_Mg = \(M_Mg * I * t\) / \(n * F\) = \(24.31 * 0.50 * 157,680,000\) / \(2 * 96,485\) =) Tj
T*
(1,916,588 / 192,970 = 9.93 kg of pure Mg.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
