T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: A glass electrode coupled to a saturated calomel electrode \(SCE, E_ref = +0.242) Tj
T*
(V\) is immersed in a fermentation broth at 25 deg C. The measured cell EMF is +0.088 V.) Tj
T*
(If the glass electrode calibration equation is E_cell = E'_glass - 0.0591 * pH - E_SCE) Tj
T*
(\(where E'_glass = +0.750 V\), calculate the exact pH of the fermentation broth.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Setup Potentiometric Equation:) Tj
T*
(E_cell = E'_glass - 0.0591 * pH - E_SCE.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Substitute Known Numerical Values:) Tj
T*
(0.088 = 0.750 - 0.0591 * pH - 0.242.) Tj
T*
